1. What does terraform init do?

terraform init initializes a Terraform working directory.

It mainly:

Downloads required providers
Downloads required modules
Configures the backend for state storage
Creates/updates the .terraform directory
Installs provider plugins


2. What does terraform validate do?
It checks whether your Terraform configuration is syntactically valid and internally consistent.
Yes, if you leave the ami value empty, Terraform will generally give you an error because ami is required for an aws_instance resource.
terraform validate
can report that the ami argument is invalid/empty.


3. What does terraform fmt do?
terraform fmt formats Terraform code into Terraform's standard style.
Example before:
resource "aws_instance" "web" {
ami="ami-123"
instance_type="t2.micro"
}
It formats it:
resource "aws_instance" "web" {
  ami           = "ami-123"
  instance_type = "t2.micro"
}

It is mainly for code formatting/readability.
Useful command:  terraform fmt -recursive
This formats Terraform files in subdirectories too.







